# GlitchTip (`burke-software-glitchtip`)

Seamlessly monitor and track app issues with GlitchTip! Experience smooth deployment on DigitalOcean or Heroku, complete with robust backend and frontend integration, plus Postgres and Redis flexibility.

[Source](https://github.com/burke-software/GlitchTip)

## Example

```terraform
resource "osc_instance" "example" {
  service_id = "burke-software-glitchtip"
  name       = "myglitchtip"

  sensitive_parameters = {
    secretKey = var.secret_key
    databaseUrl = var.database_url
  }
}
```

Commented lines are optional parameters. Values marked `"..."` need a real value. Outputs are `url`, `external_ip`, `external_port` and the raw `instance` document, see the `osc_instance` resource.

## Parameters

| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `secretKey` | string | yes | Django secret key for the GlitchTip instance; set it to a long random string of letters and keep it stable across restarts. Maps to SECRET_KEY. Sensitive, set it in `sensitive_parameters`. |
| `databaseUrl` | string | yes | PostgreSQL connection URL for GlitchTip's database, for example postgres://user:password@host:5432/dbname. Feeds DATABASE_URL. Sensitive, set it in `sensitive_parameters`. |

The instance `name` must match `^\w+$` and be unique per service within the workspace. OSC lowercases it and allows at most 20 characters.

Parameter values are strings; booleans take `"true"` or `"false"`. Reference an `osc_secret` as `osc_secret.<name>.ref` to keep a value out of the instance configuration. This page is generated from the OSC catalog; the provider validates against the live catalog when planning.
